.vs

# Clangd LSP
.cache
compile_commands.json

# Build folder -- src/Makefile's own default PROJECT_BUILD_PATH/TEST_BUILD_PATH (build/desktop/,
# build/test/, build/web/) lands here; the release CI workflows (build_linux/macos/webassembly.yml)
# also point their own PROJECT_BUILD_PATH at a sibling build/release/ now, no longer straight into
# src/ (this Makefile no longer special-cases PROJECT_BUILD_PATH=. anywhere, including its own
# `clean:` target). This one pattern covers all of it (objects, linked binaries, staged resources/,
# generated config/, GAME_MARKER, tests_runner), at any depth.
[Bb]uild

# Real files engine_config_test.cpp/game_config_test.cpp/file_io_test.cpp read/write and clean up
# around each test -- isolated from build/'s own generated config/ above so tests never collide
# with a real dev's local config. test_scratch/'s own location follows whatever directory
# tests_runner is invoked from (a plain relative path in the test sources, not derived from
# TEST_BUILD_PATH) -- test.sh/ci_sanity.yml both run it from the repo root, landing it there;
# covered both places.
/src/test_scratch/
/test_scratch/

# raylib checkout auto-vendored by build.sh
/vendor/

# Android files
*apk*
android.*

# WebAssembly release files
*.data
*.wasm
*.html
*.js
!src/minshell.html
!src/shell.html
# docs/learning/rendering.html and friends -- versioned content, not build output
!docs/**/*.html
